e fit=direct and placed in SUPPORT even if the candidate is not famous or not in the first document. A support statement is not a counter. Counter requires an explicit negative/exclusion or incompatible statement about that exact referent, and cannot be justified by absence. A birth header (date1 - date2) supports date1, not merely prose Born on. Distinct people sharing a name, distinct works with one title, multiple sports and plural mascots may legitimately coexist. Role match and truth are separate axes: competing same-role values stay direct with conflict flagged. Unknown memory is not negative evidence. Recheck all wrong_argument labels against the source before returning.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the common name for Yellow Lantern?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 186, \"text\": \"Banksia lemanniana Banksia lemanniana, commonly known as the yellow lantern banksia or Lemann's banksia, is a species of woody shrub of the family Proteaceae native to Western Australia.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 187, \"end\": 328, \"text\": \"It generally grows as an open shrub or small tree to five metres (15 ft) high with stiff serrated leaves, and unusual hanging inflorescences.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 329, \"end\": 488, \"text\": \"Flowering occurs over summer, the greenish buds developing into oval flower spikes before turning grey and developing the characteristic large woody follicles.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"start\": 489, \"end\": 593, \"text\": \"It occurs within and just east of the Fitzgerald River National Park on the southern coast of the state.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0092-abd8ca5b1126:d00\", \"